 right-hand side $f(x)≡0,$ the equation is $\\text{homogeneous}.$\n\n- The boundary conditions are\n\n$$\ny(0)=0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0.\n$$\n\nThese are $\\text{Dirichlet}$ boundary conditions, and since the right-hand sides are zero for both, they are $\\text{homogeneous}.$\n\n- Since the governing equation is homogeneous, and the boundary conditions are homogeneous, the BVP is $\\text{homogeneous}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338695/field-1" "q-338695/field-2" "q-338695/field-3" "q-338695/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af8cf798-4327-5f5b-82ab-f622f20ccc38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338695"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
